/**
* Checks if the interrupt target register contains all interrupts to be
* targeted for the current CPU. If they are programmed to be forwarded to the current CPU,
* this API disables all interrupts and disables the GIC distributor. It also removes the current CPU
* from the interrupt target registers for all interrupts.
*
* @param InstancePtr Pointer to the instance to be worked on.
*
* @return None.
*/

// Do not disable the distributor if it's already disabled.
// Track the distributor status.
// Ensure the spinlock mechanism is used to protect against concurrent writes to the same register.
// In the case of GICv3, interrupts are always routed to a fixed affinity (core 0) and cannot be unmapped.
// If any other CPU is also programmed for interrupts, the distributor cannot be disabled.
// Remove the current CPU from the interrupt target register for all interrupts.
// If the distributor is safe to be disabled, disable all interrupts and then disable the distributor.
// Release the lock previously taken if the spinlock mechanism is enabled.
